<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Taurini</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 218 BCE (approx.) · capital Taurasia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Alpine people of the upper Po whose chief town Hannibal stormed in 218 BCE and whose name lives on in Turin.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Taurini lived at the foot of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dora-riparia">Dora Riparia</a> meets the Po. Ancient writers called them Ligurian or Celtic; they were probably a Ligurian people with strong Celtic influence. Little is known of their early history.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They are known only from Greek and Roman writers. Their chief town, called Taurasia by Appian, controlled routes from the Alpine passes into the Po plain. In 218 BCE they were at war with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/insubres">Insubres</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After crossing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> in 218 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> took Taurasia in three days when its people refused his alliance, and massacred the defenders. The region later came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and Augustus founded the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Augusta Taurinorum</a> on or near the site, the origin of Turin.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/taurini.jpg" alt="Taurini" width="320" height="242"><figcaption>Image: Nancy Todd · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gallia_Cisalpina-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 218 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Taurasia</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-359&amp;focus=taurini" aria-label="Taurini on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4961 580 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taurini lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5259 1106h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5281 836h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5281 836h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Italy. <a href="/atlas?year=-359&amp;focus=taurini">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

